    "result_text": "All 279 tests pass, including the new `Cp16Tests` and the JDBC repository tests.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented `namesakeCount` on owner creation: when an owner is created, the number of other owners already sharing that last name is counted and returned in the owner response (and persisted so `GET /api/owners/{id}` returns it).\n\n**Changes:**\n\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `namesakeCount` (int32) property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gains the field.\n- **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added `namesake_count` column field with getter/setter, alongside the existing computed fields. MapStruct maps it by name automatically.\n- **`rest/function/owner/AssignNamesakeCount.java`** \u2014 new pipeline step that counts existing owners with the same last name (the new owner isn't saved yet, so every match is an \"other\" owner) and stores it on the entity, mirroring the existing `AssignCustomerCode` pattern.\n- **`officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 wired `assignNamesakeCount` into the transactional pipeline between `assignMembershipTier` and `save`.\n- **DB schemas** (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `mysql`, `postgres`) \u2014 added the `namesake_count` column; fixed the hsqldb seed `data.sql` positional inserts to include the extra `NULL`. (h2/postgres seed data use named-column inserts, so they were unaffected.)\n\nThe count runs before `save` inside the existing governed transaction, so it reflects the owner population \"at that moment\" of creation, and the persisted value is returned identically by both the POST create response and subsequent GET reads.",
